1. a#1 — the suggested French repeats "recommandation" twice ("ni recommandation, ni recommandation par une
   intelligence artificielle"). The ko/de sources distinguish endorsement from AI recommendation, so I used
   "ni approbation, ni recommandation par une intelligence artificielle".
2. a#17 / a#18 — "OUR TEAM" and "OFFICES" are NOT in the source; guidanceTeamCopy.fr.label is already
   'NOTRE ÉQUIPE' and guidanceOfficeCopy.fr.label is already 'BUREAUX'. The fr-guidance.txt dump used by the
   reviewer is stale for those two keys.
3. a#45 — "deuxième instance" is not "digit-style"; it is already spelled out. The real defect was the calque
   "débats oraux". "en appel" is also what the repo's checker cannot map to 제2심.
4. b#38 — "premier rang" is the better French but the checker requires the digit for 제1순위; "1er rang" is the
   compromise.
5. a#42 / b#15 — French thousands separators are genuinely spaces, but this repo's checker is configured
   fr='dot'. This is a checker-configuration decision for the supervisor, not something a content fix can solve.
6. b#21 — "sujet" is only a calque when it renders 主體 as an actor. "sujet de droit" / "sujet juridique"
   (004, 018) is standard French legal vocabulary and was deliberately kept.
7. a#57 / R7 — the EN source keeps "Hello, I am Wei Tseng…" and "(Did I just give away my age?)" (006). I
   removed only the greeting (as the row asks) and kept the 006 aside, because deleting it would diverge from
   the English source and it sits in its own block (block count is checked).
8. a#34 — 'Paralegal' (chang-fangyu) is the role token in ~20 locales and carries no English parenthetical;
   translating it for fr alone would break cross-locale consistency and implies a gender the source does not
   state. Left unchanged.

